! brief-common.md — brief, 2026-10-26

Verbatim scratch record `.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/brief-common.md` (brief, file date 2026-10-26); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext, its words kept as written. Index: [[workshop index|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/workshop/research/k15-bonds/index]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in your seat dir. No git writes,
no suites. Web allowed: cite URLs. Mark MEASURED (file:line) vs LEAD (your reading).

GROUND. Code in /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine at the span head (read only). The ruling, road
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem :208 ("Custody and identity read by capability, never by host",
operator, 2026-10-19): a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join,
enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place
signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; a faceless
vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private. "A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and
group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (open-node-vessel.ts), and a browser's do the same
(open-browser-vessel.ts); each is a bond owed, carried by K15." Also :207 (a shared act never makes a shared secret; D/F/S
sort), the K15 row (:459), kits docs/pono/k15-wave-{c,d}-lane.mem, k15-custody-step-zero.mem, w29-place-kel-lane.mem
&#35;/owed, and THE CENSUS: tools/seed-census.mjs (its named K15 exceptions: the Keyhive Individual and ContactCard
(place-card.ts, ceremony-core), the bare place leaf (leaf-identity.ts), the relay key (open-node-vessel.ts,
carriage-relay.ts), daemon auth, device and face work, internal asks, lares-cli meme.ts signing).

THE TASK: map every K15 bond to its end state before a lane builds it (build the end state; a lane that hardens an
unruled assumption costs more than the wait). For EACH census exception:
# MEASURE what reads the seed today and what it signs or opens, for whom, on node and browser (file:line).
# NAME its replacement under the ruling: the face's atom (which face, chosen how, when a vessel wears several or none),
the scoped place signer (only if a floor duty), a per-purpose key minted at random in a sealed row (D or S, whose
FCK), or retirement. Quote the canon that rules it, or say "derived" and name the house law, or "operator" with
options and one lean.
# THE BYTES: does it move identity or format bytes (so it precedes X0)? What wire or stored shape changes?
# THE ORDER and FILES: dependencies between bonds, the files each holds, and overlap with the running lanes (W14-W16:
place-floor-pin, admit-gate-pin, hearth-gate-pins, herm-carriage, nexus-contract, carry-bundle, browser-gate-pins,
browser-floor-read, open-browser-vessel card filing, web main.ts/live-status.ts; D2: tw5 port/island protocol,
hand-gate, tw5-projection, web projection-sink, open-node-vessel port hunks; G15: afterRollChain in open-node-vessel,
build-plugin-tiddler). One lane or several, and why.
# The faceless vessel: what a vessel that wears no face (a bare herm, a floor-only node) signs with, and what refuses.
# Reds: for each bond, the red (a place seed yields no face proof, no Keyhive Individual, no daemon authority, no relay
identity, no meme signature), its control and known positive.
Prior art on the web: KERI delegated identifiers, Keyhive/Beelay individual vs group keys, Signal device keys,
Matrix cross-signing (device vs user keys), WebAuthn per-RP keys. What fits?
House laws: no global now; build the end state; one name, one relation; isomorphic by intent; the herm carries and
never reads; silent-zero; evergreen; never "family" for a PersonaGroup.

